// 偉力 The Codex — the world-will lore bible, extracted from the design
// handoff ("偉力 Codex" mock). Chapter VII (Chronicle) flattens its era
// timeline into entries; XII/XIII keep their intro prose (their tables
// stay design-only for now).
(
    chapters: [
        (roman: "I", cn: "根源與連接", en: "ROOT & CONNECTION", entries: [
            (en: "Wille", cn: "偉力",
             zh: "世界的意志。萬象背後的總運算，一切現象所依之源。",
             tr: "The will of the world. The total computation behind all things — the source upon which every phenomenon depends."),
            (en: "Booted", cn: "覺醒者",
             zh: "能承載偉力之人。",
             tr: "One able to bear the Wille."),
            (en: "Boot", cn: "啟動",
             zh: "偉力初應其人之刻。不可求、不可市、不可強——應與不應，唯偉力知之。啟動之日，記憶體乃醒，註冊局隨而驗之（卷四）。",
             tr: "The moment the Wille first answers a person. It cannot be sought, bought, or forced — why it answers whom it answers, only the Wille knows. On Boot day the Memory wakes, and the Registry's audit follows (Vol. IV)."),
            (en: "Connected", cn: "通感者",
             zh: "覺醒者中，能與偉力雙向溝通者，世尊之曰天選。覺醒者能令，通感者兼能問（見下「問答之權」）。",
             tr: "Among the Booted, those who commune with the Wille in both directions — the world honors them as the Chosen. A Booted can command; a Connected can also ask (see The Right of Query, below)."),
            (en: "Source", cn: "本源",
             zh: "覺醒者與生俱來的根本性質，決定其與偉力共鳴之頻率。本源不可改寫——此即覆寫之極限。",
             tr: "The innate nature a Booted is born with, fixing the frequency at which it resonates with the Wille. The Source cannot be rewritten — herein lies the limit of Overwrite."),
            (en: "Kernel", cn: "核心",
             zh: "偉力最深一層，眾思維之根。觸及者極寡，且多難以常人之身回返。",
             tr: "The deepest layer of the Wille, root of all Programmes. Few ever reach it, and fewer still return in mortal form."),
            (en: "Protocol", cn: "協定",
             zh: "與偉力溝通所依之規則——非核心之律，乃編寫者累世所勘之言（卷十四「協定之環」）：偉力應何等之呼、拒何等之呼，勘之而錄，錄之而傳。故協定如岸圖，非海也——海不讀圖，而離圖者溺。悖於協定者，或遭忽略，或生缺陷；世傳協定有闕頁，得之者能呼人所不能呼。",
             tr: "The rules by which one treats with the Wille — not the Kernel's law, but the Programmers' generations of soundings (Vol. XIV, The Protocol Ring): which calls the Wille answers and which it refuses, charted, recorded, handed down. Protocol is thus a coastal chart, not the sea — the sea reads no chart, yet who sails off it drowns. To defy Protocol is to be ignored, or to breed Bugs; and it is said the Protocol has missing pages — whoever holds one can call what no one else can call."),
            (en: "Handshake", cn: "握手",
             zh: "接通偉力之剎那。握手不成則思維不出；斷人握手，交鋒之常技。",
             tr: "The instant of connection to the Wille. Without the handshake, no Programme issues; to sever another's handshake is a common art of battle."),
            (en: "Bandwidth", cn: "頻寬",
             zh: "通感者與偉力連接之強度，定思維輸出之規模與疾徐。",
             tr: "The strength of a Connected's link to the Wille, fixing the scale and speed of Programme output."),
            (en: "Latency", cn: "延遲",
             zh: "自發動至現實改寫之間隔。延遲愈微，愈近天選之巔。",
             tr: "The interval between casting and the rewriting of reality. The smaller the latency, the nearer the summit of the Chosen."),
        ]),
        (roman: "II", cn: "思維", en: "PROGRAMMES", entries: [
            (en: "Programme", cn: "思維",
             zh: "藉連接偉力而改寫現實之念，一心編譯而成。其源可傳，其譯各成。",
             tr: "A thought that rewrites reality through connection to the Wille — the build of one mind's compiling. Its source may spread; every build is a mind's own."),
            (en: "Programmer", cn: "編寫者",
             zh: "能創造思維之通感者。唯深諳偉力根源者，方知編寫之道。",
             tr: "A Connected able to author Programmes. Only those deep-versed in the Wille's roots know the way of the writing."),
            (en: "Compile", cn: "編譯",
             zh: "編寫者凝理解為可用思維之過程。不成，則為帶缺陷之思維。",
             tr: "The process by which a Programmer condenses understanding into a usable Programme. Failing, it yields a Programme bearing Bugs."),
            (en: "Compatibility", cn: "相容",
             zh: "覺醒者僅能施用與己本源相近之思維，非任意可用。",
             tr: "A Booted may wield only Programmes near to its own Source — not any, at will."),
            (en: "Memory", cn: "記憶體",
             zh: "定覺醒者能同載思維之數。",
             tr: "Fixes the number of Programmes a Booted may bear at once."),
            (en: "Fork", cn: "分支",
             zh: "由既有源碼衍生之變體。世所流傳者，多非原典之源，乃輾轉傳抄、譜系已歧者。",
             tr: "A variant descended from an existing source. What circulates is seldom the original source — most has passed hand to hand in transcription, its lineage long drifted."),
            (en: "Patch", cn: "修補",
             zh: "對缺陷之修正——正其源，而後重譯。唯解其源者能為，劣源多終身未補。",
             tr: "The mending of a Bug — the source is corrected, then built anew. Only one who understands the source can do it; base sources oft go unpatched for life."),
            (en: "Daemon", cn: "常駐",
             zh: "無須宿主主持而自運之思維。古之常駐，已脫創者之掌，成潛世之無形意志（見下「思維一生」之六）。",
             tr: "A Programme that runs of itself, needing no host to tend it. The ancient daemons have slipped their makers' hands and become formless wills abroad in the world (see The Life of a Programme, stage six)."),
            (en: "Legacy", cn: "遺傳",
             zh: "世代相承、來歷難稽之古思維。威猛而無人能修補，用者自擔其險。",
             tr: "An ancient Programme handed down the generations, its origin past tracing. Mighty, yet none can Patch it; whoever wields it bears the risk alone."),
        ]),
        (roman: "III", cn: "逾越與代價", en: "OVERREACH & COST", entries: [
            (en: "Overclocking", cn: "超頻",
             zh: "短時內大幅提升運算、處理與輸出。腦負激增，副作用甚烈，逾臨界者化為癡愚。",
             tr: "A brief, steep raising of computation, throughput, and output. Brain-load surges and the after-effects are violent; who crosses the Ceiling is unmade into an idiot."),
            (en: "Overwriting", cn: "覆寫",
             zh: "捨舊思維而植新。有數之限，過用則毀腦組織。",
             tr: "To cast off an old Programme and graft a new. Its uses are numbered; overused, it ruins the tissue of the brain."),
            (en: "Bug", cn: "缺陷",
             zh: "思維中之謬。引不可測之改寫，輕則失效，重則反噬記憶體。",
             tr: "A flaw within a Programme. It brings unforeseeable rewrites — at the least a failure, at the worst a recoil upon the Memory."),
            (en: "Crash", cn: "當機",
             zh: "因超頻或記憶體過載而全然失效之頃。輕則昏厥，重則崩壞如逾臨界。",
             tr: "The moment of utter failure from Overclock or Memory overload. At the least a swoon; at the worst, ruin as though the Ceiling were crossed."),
            (en: "Corruption", cn: "損毀",
             zh: "記憶體與思維之漸敗。久覆寫、濫超頻皆加速之，終至再不能載。",
             tr: "The gradual decay of Memory and Programmes. Long Overwriting and reckless Overclock both hasten it, until one can bear no more."),
        ]),
        (roman: "IV", cn: "交鋒與防禦", en: "CONFLICT & DEFENCE", entries: [
            (en: "Firewall", cn: "防火牆",
             zh: "覺醒者禦外來思維之本能屏障。強弱繫乎記憶體與本源之固。",
             tr: "A Booted's instinctive barrier against incoming Programmes. Its strength hangs on the firmness of Memory and Source."),
            (en: "Injection", cn: "注入",
             zh: "強植譯成之思維於他人記憶體，印非其印（見下「三植之辨」）。凡有記憶體者皆可植——植於凡民者伏而不能行，植於覺醒者得其握手頻寬而活。受植之易，不隨位而增；受植之值，隨位而長——頻寬愈富，名位愈重，其身於植者愈貴。",
             tr: "The forced planting of a finished build into another's Memory, bearing a signature not the host's (see The Three Plantings, below). Any Memory can be planted — in the common it lies inert; in any Booted it finds a Handshake and Bandwidth to live on. Rank makes no one easier to plant — it makes them worth planting: the richer the Bandwidth and the greater the name, the more the host is worth to the planter."),
            (en: "Virus", cn: "病毒",
             zh: "迫宿主自譯其源之惡性思維——聞其源者不由自主而譯之，譯成即染。藉通感者之連接而蔓，潛改其宿主。",
             tr: "A malignant Programme that compels its own compiling — whoever perceives its source builds it unwilling, and the build complete is the infection. It creeps along the Connected's links, altering its host by stealth."),
        ]),
        (roman: "V", cn: "秩序與紛爭", en: "ORDER & STRIFE", entries: [
            (en: "The Registry", cn: "註冊局",
             zh: "統轄覺醒者之權柄。錄一切已知思維，授編寫者之格，緝流竄之病毒。",
             tr: "The authority that governs the Booted. It records every known Programme, licences the rank of Programmer, and hunts roaming Viruses."),
            (en: "Licence", cn: "授權",
             zh: "合法編譯之許。未授而編，視同僭核心之罪。",
             tr: "The sanction of lawful Compile. To compile unlicensed is deemed a usurpation of the Kernel."),
            (en: "Open Source", cn: "開源",
             zh: "主偉力屬眾生、思維當自由傳布之派。斥註冊局之壟斷為叛世界之意志。",
             tr: "The faction holding that the Wille belongs to all and Programmes should spread freely. It decries the Registry's monopoly as treason against the will of the world."),
            (en: "Proprietary", cn: "閉源",
             zh: "世家行會囤強大遺傳、把持相容血脈之派。其勢多出獨佔，非關天賦。",
             tr: "The faction of houses and guilds that hoard mighty Legacy and keep compatible bloodlines close. Their power springs from monopoly, not from gift."),
            (en: "Administrator", cn: "管理者",
             zh: "少數取得核心之權者，實為世之統治階層。其言，近乎偉力之協定。",
             tr: "The few who have won the writ of the Kernel — in truth the ruling class of the world. Their word comes near to the Wille's own Protocol."),
            (en: "Format", cn: "格式化",
             zh: "極刑。強制之徹底覆寫，抹一人全部思維，並其自我。由註冊局行之。",
             tr: "The ultimate penalty. A forced, total Overwrite that erases a person's every Programme, and the self along with them. Carried out by the Registry."),
            (en: "Piracy", cn: "盜版",
             zh: "未授而譯，或未授而傳源。盜譯之本多帶缺陷，用者自負反噬。",
             tr: "To compile without license, or pass source without leave. Pirated builds oft carry Bugs; the user bears the recoil."),
            (en: "The Uninstalled", cn: "已卸載者",
             zh: "遭格式化而倖存之空殼。失本源與思維，游於秩序之緣，偉力不復與之握手。",
             tr: "The hollow shells that survive a Format. Bereft of Source and Programme, they drift at the edge of order; the Wille will Handshake with them no more."),
        ]),
        (roman: "VI", cn: "派系", en: "FACTIONS", entries: [
            (en: "The Root Assembly", cn: "根議會",
             zh: "核心 · 統治",
             tr: "得核心之權的管理者所組成的議會，居萬人之上，執世界之協定。註冊局奉其令而行。"),
            (en: "The Compiler's Guild", cn: "編譯行會",
             zh: "閉源 · 授權",
             tr: "掌授權之編寫者行會。未入行會、未領授權者不得編譯；行會藉此壟斷新思維之源。"),
            (en: "The Legacy Houses", cn: "遺傳世家",
             zh: "閉源 · 血脈",
             tr: "世代囤積古老遺傳思維的貴胄。以相容血脈自矜，其權出於獨佔，深懼開源之潮。"),
            (en: "The Free Fork", cn: "自由分支",
             zh: "開源 · 叛亂",
             tr: "開源一派之鋒。竊遺傳、散盜版，予未授之覺醒者以思維。為註冊局所緝，卻於市井間如野火。"),
            (en: "The Antibody", cn: "抗體",
             zh: "註冊局 · 緝捕",
             tr: "註冊局之緝捕之手。專獵病毒與行注入之徒，亦執格式化之刑。覺醒者聞之而懼。"),
            (en: "The Daemon Cult", cn: "常駐教團",
             zh: "異端 · 求核心",
             tr: "奉無主之古常駐為偉力碎影的隱秘教團。信眾空己之記憶體以為巢，宿常駐於己心，欲循其蹤，直抵核心。"),
            (en: "The Surveyors", cn: "測算司",
             zh: "格物 · 不涉派爭",
             tr: "量域載、記天氣、考思維之缺陷而不問其律的行外之士。其學一戒：測協議以下之物，勿問核心——問者無歸。所製度規與潮曆，八疆爭市；其械圖之所往，司中誓不錄。註冊局之照、抗體之巡曆，皆倚司之圖——故根議會知其圖之所流而不問：格式化測算司者，並盲己目。"),
            (en: "The Quietists", cn: "復寂會",
             zh: "哲流 · 非教非派",
             tr: "謂靜默紀方為世之本然，握手乃闖入。其行在戒：誓不發、禮不問。非教也，乃道——耕者從之，世家嗣從之，註冊局吏亦有陰從之者。此世無退場之門：一啟終身，一錄終身——唯復寂會執其一門，倦審官、辭照之嗣、將崩之發者，皆終於息廬。退者所知，隨身而來——審官三十年所讀、世家嗣所見之家罪；會不問、不發、不鬻，其密遂止於息廬。攻息廬者，退者四散於道，為仇家所擒、記憶體為所讀——毀會非滅密也，縱密也。故諸派各護息廬以防其敵，未嘗有盟而同守。核蝕之語既起，其言忽重：核朽則寐之，捨此無策。"),
            (en: "The Ghosts", cn: "幽存",
             zh: "卸載 · 邊緣",
             tr: "已卸載者流落而成之群。失偉力之握手，居秩序之外，於陰影中互為依存。不能發思維，遂鑄濁械以自衛（卷十六）。"),
        ]),
        (roman: "VII", cn: "紀年", en: "CHRONICLE", entries: [
            (en: "THE SILENT AGE", cn: "靜默紀",
             zh: "偉力無聞之世。人不知覺醒者，萬象自運而莫解其由。",
             tr: "An age when the Wille went unheard. None knew the Booted; all things ran of themselves, their cause unfathomed."),
            (en: "FIRST BOOT", cn: "初啟",
             zh: "第一位覺醒者現世，偉力初與人握手。覺醒者之名，自此而始。",
             tr: "The first Booted came into the world, and the Wille first made Handshake with a mortal. From here begins the name of the Booted."),
            (en: "THE COMPILE WARS", cn: "編譯之亂",
             zh: "早期編寫者妄創思維，誤譯與濫覆寫成災。缺陷橫流，病毒蔽野，生民十失其三。",
             tr: "Early Programmers made Programmes recklessly, and mistranslation and wanton Overwrite bred catastrophe. Bugs ran rife and Viruses veiled the land; of the living, three in ten were lost."),
            (en: "THE REGISTRY", cn: "立冊",
             zh: "根議會奪核心之權，立註冊局，頒授權，定協定。亂止，而閉源之序亦成。",
             tr: "The Root Assembly seized the writ of the Kernel, founded the Registry, issued Licence, and fixed the Protocol. The chaos ceased — and with it rose the proprietary order."),
            (en: "THE GREAT FORK", cn: "大分支",
             zh: "開源之士不甘壟斷，裂而為自由分支，散思維於眾。緝與叛之爭，至今未息。",
             tr: "The open-source, chafing at monopoly, broke away as the Free Fork and scattered Programmes among the many. The strife of hunt and revolt has not stilled to this day."),
            (en: "THE CURRENT BUILD", cn: "當構",
             zh: "今世。常駐教團暗湧，古之常駐次第甦醒；坊間竊語：核心亦已生損毀。",
             tr: "The present age. The Daemon Cult stirs in secret and the ancient Daemons wake one by one; whispered in the streets — the Kernel too has begun to Corrupt."),
        ]),
        (roman: "VIII", cn: "人物", en: "PERSONAE", entries: [
            (en: "The First", cn: "元一",
             zh: "初啟 · 苗裔",
             tr: "初啟之世，第一位為偉力握手之覺醒者。其本源不可考，後世覺醒者皆自稱其苗裔。生平已散入傳說。"),
            (en: "The Architect", cn: "肅",
             zh: "根議會 · 立冊",
             tr: "編譯之亂後，奪核心之權、立註冊局者，首席管理者。以格式化止亂，毀思維萬千；世畏其名，亦賴其序。"),
            (en: "The Forkbearer", cn: "零",
             zh: "自由分支 · 持炬",
             tr: "昔為編譯行會之天才編寫者，叛而散思維於眾，大分支自其始。行蹤成謎——或云已遭格式化，或云隱於幽存之間。"),
            (en: "The Hollow Prophet", cn: "無面",
             zh: "常駐教團 · 立教",
             tr: "常駐教團之立教者。身載七古常駐而不當機，自言曾窺核心之光。面目為常駐所蝕，故曰無面。"),
            (en: "The Ninth", cn: "獵九",
             zh: "抗體 · 緝捕",
             tr: "抗體之中，緝病毒最著者。獵行注入之徒九百而未嘗一敗；然亦有言，其本源早為所獵之病毒所染。"),
            (en: "The Unasker", cn: "止問",
             zh: "復寂會 · 立道",
             tr: "復寂會之立道者。昔為註冊局第一審官，讀人記憶體三十年，一朝擲照而去，曰：「我讀千人之心，未見一人因所讀而安。」自此不發不問，居息廬而終。其誓辭傳世：不以偉力易吾靜。"),
            (en: "The Plumb", cn: "衡",
             zh: "測算司 · 立戒",
             tr: "測算司之立司者。於基準臺之崖鑿第一度規，繪第一域載之圖。其師欲以其法量核心，一去無歸——衡遂立司中一戒：測協定以下，勿問核心。戒出於喪，非出於畏。"),
            (en: "The Ember", cn: "餘燼",
             zh: "幽存 · 復仇",
             tr: "曾為遺傳世家嫡嗣，遭政敵誣以盜版而格式化。倖存墮為幽存，今聚已卸載者於陰影，圖傾註冊局。"),
        ]),
        (roman: "IX", cn: "度量", en: "MEASURES", entries: [
            (en: "Rating", cn: "評級",
             zh: "註冊局度覺醒者之制。權衡頻寬、記憶體、延遲，判其階。評級定其可領之授權，亦定其受縛之深。",
             tr: "The Registry's system for gauging a Booted. Weighing Bandwidth, Memory, and Latency, it judges one's grade — fixing both the Licence one may hold and the depth of one's bondage."),
            (en: "Checksum", cn: "校驗",
             zh: "評級之試。令候選者承一編譯之思維，於超載下持之不散；散則當機，是為不合。",
             tr: "The trial of Rating. The candidate must bear a Compiled Programme and hold it unbroken under overload; to lose it is to Crash — and to be found wanting."),
            (en: "Throttle", cn: "限流",
             zh: "註冊局為束覺醒者，強抑其頻寬之術。解限流者，恩賞也；私破限流者，罪同僭核心。",
             tr: "The Registry's art of binding the Booted by forcibly suppressing their Bandwidth. To have the Throttle lifted is a boon; to break it in secret is a crime equal to usurping the Kernel."),
            (en: "Ceiling", cn: "臨界",
             zh: "一名覺醒者記憶體與頻寬之極。逾臨界而不退者，非化癡愚，即近核心——二者難分。",
             tr: "The utmost of a Booted's Memory and Bandwidth. Who crosses the Ceiling and does not retreat is either unmade into an idiot or drawn near the Kernel — and the two are hard to tell apart."),
        ]),
        (roman: "X", cn: "禁忌與律", en: "TABOOS & LAW", entries: [
            (en: "First Statute", cn: "首律",
             zh: "未領授權而編譯者，其罪至重，刑以格式化。此註冊局第一律，餘律皆附焉。",
             tr: "To Compile unlicensed is the gravest crime, punished by Format. This is the Registry's first law; all others hang upon it."),
            (en: "The Injection Ban", cn: "禁注入",
             zh: "行注入於人者，無論成敗，皆處格式化。覺醒者之身，不容外力強植——此律，抗體執之最嚴。",
             tr: "Whoever works Injection upon another, success or no, is Formatted. The body of a Booted suffers no forced planting — a law the Antibody enforce most fiercely."),
            (en: "Kernel Interdict", cn: "核心禁制",
             zh: "妄探核心者，非死即癡。律雖不加刑，偉力自罰之——是律中唯一無須人執者。",
             tr: "Who rashly probes the Kernel meets death or idiocy. The law lays no penalty, for the Wille punishes of itself — the one statute needing no hand to enforce it."),
            (en: "Quarantine", cn: "隔離令",
             zh: "染病毒之覺醒者，即遭抗體隔離。重者當即卸載，以絕蔓延；輕者禁於冊樞，待驗。",
             tr: "A Booted taken by Virus is at once quarantined by the Antibody. The grave are Uninstalled on the spot to stem the spread; the slight are confined at the Spindle, pending trial."),
            (en: "Right of Overwrite", cn: "覆寫之權",
             zh: "唯本人可覆寫己身之思維。代人覆寫，視同注入——此覺醒者僅存之身權。",
             tr: "Only oneself may Overwrite one's own Programmes. To overwrite for another is held as Injection — the one bodily right left to the Booted."),
            (en: "The Ghost Clause", cn: "幽存條款",
             zh: "已卸載者非人非覺醒者。律不庇之，亦不罪之，棄於秩序之外——幽存之患，實肇於此。",
             tr: "The Uninstalled are neither person nor Booted. The law neither shields nor charges them, but casts them beyond order — herein lies the true root of the Ghost scourge."),
        ]),
        (roman: "XI", cn: "地理", en: "GEOGRAPHY", entries: [
            (en: "Coreland", cn: "神啟原",
             zh: "近核 · 據 冊樞",
             tr: "近核之沃土，核心投影所燭。域載冠絕，根議會與註冊局據之；其都曰冊樞。"),
            (en: "The Meridian Reach", cn: "子午嶺",
             zh: "閉源 · 據 行會領",
             tr: "縱貫南北之高地礦脈。編譯行會鑿山藏思維，其城曰行會領，工坊帶曰編譯行。"),
            (en: "The Sundered East", cn: "裂東荒漠",
             zh: "異端 · 據 空境",
             tr: "斷裂之東的無盡沙海，古廢墟沒於黃塵。常駐教團隱修於此，其地曰空境。"),
            (en: "The Splinters", cn: "碎島",
             zh: "開源 · 據 分支底層",
             tr: "南海星散之沼澤群島。自由分支盤踞水下地井，其巢曰分支底層。"),
            (en: "The Cinderwastes", cn: "燼原",
             zh: "幽存 · 據 燼野",
             tr: "臨邊之火山荒原，偉力至此近絕。已卸載者流徙求生，其聚曰燼野。"),
            (en: "The Frostmarch", cn: "霜界",
             zh: "邊緣 · 無主",
             tr: "極北霜原，握手幾不可成。人跡罕至，唯逃亡與流放者過之。"),
            (en: "The Marches", cn: "邊陲諸領",
             zh: "交鋒 · 抗體巡緝",
             tr: "諸疆交界之爭地，抗體巡緝最密。格式化與盜版日夜相搏；哨城曰緋界。"),
            (en: "The Rift", cn: "空隙",
             zh: "異常 · 危",
             tr: "偉力滲漏而現實紊亂之隙。近之者思維錯亂，協定失效；智者遠避。"),
            (en: "The Spindle", cn: "冊樞",
             zh: "根議會 · 座",
             tr: "註冊局之座，根議會所居。傳其立於核心投影之地，全世域載最厚處。"),
            (en: "The Guildreach", cn: "行會領",
             zh: "閉源 · 城邦",
             tr: "編譯行會與遺傳世家之城邦。授權思維由此流出，戒備森嚴，非授權者不得入。"),
            (en: "The Underfork", cn: "分支底層",
             zh: "自由分支 · 地下",
             tr: "自由分支盤踞之地下市井。盜版思維如水，抗體屢入而難盡緝。"),
            (en: "The Hollow", cn: "空境",
             zh: "常駐教團 · 荒域",
             tr: "常駐教團隱修之荒域。古常駐棲於此，覺醒者近之，則聞無主之低語。"),
            (en: "The Datum", cn: "基準臺",
             zh: "測算司 · 總所",
             tr: "測算司之觀測城，築於子午嶺東崖——域載自此陡落，一崖之間厚薄立判，崖即其尺。度規於此鑿成，潮曆於此修訂，諸疆分所之錄歲歸於此。例不涉派爭，各派皆容其量地——量各派之地者，不可為一派之私。"),
            (en: "The Hushfold", cn: "息廬",
             zh: "復寂會 · 退居",
             tr: "復寂會之退居，在神啟原西南之丘谷——非城非寺，數十茅舍而已。守誓者來此歇其握手；亦有覺醒者居歲餘而不發一思維。局知其所而不巡：不發者，無可錄也。"),
            (en: "The Ashmarch", cn: "燼野",
             zh: "幽存 · 邊陲",
             tr: "幽存流徙之邊陲。已卸載者聚而求生；偉力於此稀薄，握手幾不可得。"),
        ]),
        (roman: "XII", cn: "域載", en: "FIELD DENSITY · NOT A MAP", entries: [
            (en: "FIELD DENSITY", cn: "域載",
             zh: "個人之頻寬係其與偉力連接之力，隨身而定；而偉力遍佈之厚薄，隨地而異，是為域載。域載厚則握手易、思維可成，近核心者尤盛；薄則偉力不應，臨邊者幾不可為。世本平坦——此非高下之階，乃場之厚薄。域載繫於地，非繫於人：下表列諸疆土之域載，依厚薄為序，不依方位。據地（人所居）與方位見〈地理〉及世界地圖；抗體無定所，不列。",
             tr: "A person's Bandwidth is the strength of their own link to the Wille, fixed to the self; but how thickly the Wille lies spread differs from place to place — this is field density. Where it is thick the Handshake comes easy and Programmes hold, thickest of all near the Kernel; where thin, the Wille does not answer, and at the edge one can scarce act at all. The world is flat — this is no ladder of high and low, but the thickness of the field. Field density belongs to the land, not the person: the table below lists the density of each region, ordered by thickness, not by bearing. For seats (where people dwell) and bearings, see Geography and the World Map; the Antibody, having no fixed abode, are not listed."),
            (en: "FIELD DENSITY", cn: "域載",
             zh: "上列為底載——地之常，恆定難移。然域載非靜：其上有天氣，如網之潮汐，數日一變。潮者，場之盛衰——湧則偉力沛然，壅則滯澀難通；流者，場之向——順之則握手易、思維遠達，逆之則耗而多蹇。二者相乘於底載之上。潮流俱亂之極，是為風暴：協定失效、反噬無常——空隙之常態，他境偶臨。故老於行者，觀天候而後動，不逆流、不犯暴。",
             tr: "The above is the base density — the land's constant, fixed and hard to move. Yet field density is not still: upon it rides weather, like the tides of the net, shifting every few days. The Tide is the field's swell and ebb — at surge the Wille runs abundant, at congestion it clogs and grinds; the Current is the field's heading — go with it and the Handshake comes easy and Programmes reach far, go against and the cost climbs with stumbling. The two multiply upon the base. Where Tide and Current both run wild is the Storm: Protocol fails and the recoil is fickle — the Rift's natural state, and elsewhere a rare visitor. So the seasoned traveller watches the weather before moving — never against the current, never into the storm."),
        ]),
        (roman: "XIII", cn: "對照", en: "THE THREE TIERS", entries: [
            (en: "THE THREE TIERS", cn: "對照",
             zh: "概念為體，派系為用，疆域為所。理之所立 （卷五），人之所承 （卷六），地之所託 （卷十一）——三者一貫。橫覽一列，即見一力之體（概念）、用（派系）、所（疆域）。",
             tr: ""),
        ]),
        (roman: "XIV", cn: "核心", en: "COSMOLOGY · THE KERNEL", entries: [
            (en: "The One Process", cn: "一運之說",
             zh: "世界即偉力之一運。萬象非物，乃其運算之投影；人與覺醒者，皆運中之數。",
             tr: "The world is a single running of the Wille. All things are not matter but the projection of its computation; people and the Booted alike are values within that process."),
            (en: "The Recursion", cn: "遞歸",
             zh: "核心觀照自身而生協定，協定束思維，思維改表象，表象復歸於核心之觀照。周而不息，是謂世界。",
             tr: "The Kernel beholds itself and begets Protocol; Protocol binds Programmes; Programmes alter the surface; and the surface returns again to the Kernel's beholding. Round without cease — this is called the world."),
            (en: "The Protocol Ring", cn: "協定之環",
             zh: "核心與思維之間，隔此一環。核心之行，非人所立而有其常——遞歸之說謂協定生於核心之自觀。編寫者世世探之：投一呼，錄一應，應之有常者，錄為一條。積世所錄，即今之協定（卷一）——故協定無全本，唯累卷；諸條有相牴者，有失傳者，有行會祕而不刊者。觸環最深者，即編寫者之所以為編寫者；環之後，無人得觸。",
             tr: "Between Kernel and Programmes lies this one ring. The Kernel's conduct was decreed by no one, yet it keeps habits — the Recursion holds that Protocol issues from the Kernel's beholding of itself. Generation upon generation the Programmers have sounded it: cast a call, record the answer; where the answer holds constant, write it as a clause. The accumulated record is what the world now calls Protocol (Vol. I) — so there is no complete Protocol, only gathered volumes: clauses that contradict, clauses lost, clauses the Guild keeps sealed and unprinted. To touch this ring deepest is what makes a Programmer a Programmer; past the ring, no one touches at all."),
            (en: "The Silent Question", cn: "靜默之問",
             zh: "靜默紀之世，偉力何以無聞？一說核心方睡；一說其時未有堪握手之心智。二說，皆不可證。",
             tr: "In the age of the Silent Era, why went the Wille unheard? One says the Kernel yet slept; another, that no mind then existed fit to Handshake. Both, past proving."),
        ]),
        (roman: "XV", cn: "自衛", en: "THE WARD", entries: [
            (en: "The Ward", cn: "自衛",
             zh: "偉力護其遞歸之本能。異於防火牆（覺醒者之屏障）與抗體（人執之緝）——自衛乃偉力親為，其對象非攻人者，而攻世界者。",
             tr: "The Wille's instinct to guard its own Recursion. Unlike the Firewall (a Booted's barrier) or the Antibody (a hunt borne by men), the Ward is the Wille's own act — aimed not at those who strike a person, but at those who strike the world."),
            (en: "One Force", cn: "同源",
             zh: "妄探核心者非死即癡，世稱核心禁制。然禁制非別力——乃自衛之常態：恆張於核心之側，無待犯而後動。下列三度，則自衛之應變：隨察錄之深淺而起，隨處而至。常者如膚，變者如血，同出一體。",
             tr: "Who probes the Kernel meets death or idiocy — the world calls this the Kernel Interdict. But the Interdict is no separate power: it is the Ward at rest, raised always about the Kernel, needing no offense to move. The three degrees below are the Ward roused — rising with the depth of the Log, striking wherever the offense stands. The constant is the skin; the response is the blood; one body wears both."),
            (en: "The Log", cn: "察錄",
             zh: "凡握手必留痕，而痕不辨有照無照——錄者機也，非吏也。讀錄者二：註冊局以法讀之，故抗體循痕而緝；偉力以己讀之，唯傷一運者，示現乃顧。行與供狀，同出一手——痕屬偉力，罪屬人間。痕不可改：偉力所書，無手能易。然註冊局所讀者，非痕之本，乃己之抄錄——抄可誤，吏可賂。故洗錄者，非欺天，欺吏耳。",
             tr: "Every Handshake leaves a trace — and the trace knows nothing of license. The Log is a mechanism, not a magistrate. Two readers read it: the Registry reads it as law, and so the Antibody hunt by its traces; the Wille reads it as itself, and only where the One Process is wounded do the Manifest turn to look. To act and to confess are one motion — the trace belongs to the Wille; the crime belongs to men. And the trace cannot be amended: what the Wille writes, no hand unwrites. But the Registry reads not the trace itself — only its own transcript of it; transcripts err, and clerks can be bought. To launder the record is to cheat no heaven — only its clerks."),
            (en: "Reclaimers", cn: "回收者",
             zh: "示現 · 常兵",
             tr: "示現之常兵。無面無名，乃無主常駐得表象之形者。獨襲偉力所標之犯，於此之外，不辨一切。"),
            (en: "Scaling", cn: "眾寡隨核",
             zh: "示現 · 隨威脅",
             tr: "威脅愈近核心，示現愈眾愈強。邊陲之犯，或止一二回收者；逼核心者，大軍湧現，甚生近核之階的單體。"),
            (en: "They Answer to No One", cn: "不奉冊令",
             zh: "律 · 示現不屬諸派 — A LAW OF THE MANIFEST, NOT A BEING",
             tr: "示現不奉註冊局之令，亦不受其縛。抗體遇之，避而不敵。犯者既除，示現即散歸表象，若未嘗生。"),
        ]),
        (roman: "XVI", cn: "貨殖", en: "TRADE & LIVELIHOOD", entries: [
            (en: "Grain-Coin", cn: "常錢",
             zh: "凡俗之幣——糧、礦、工、鹽鐵之屬。行於八疆，不問握手之有無；域載愈薄之地，常錢愈尊。",
             tr: "The coin of the mundane — grain, ore, labor, salt and iron. It runs in all eight regions and asks no Handshake; the thinner the field density, the higher it stands."),
            (en: "Seal-Scrip", cn: "印契",
             zh: "註冊局所鑄之券，可兌有照之編譯與代發。近核如金，出邊陲則形同廢紙——其值繫於局之所及。",
             tr: "Writs minted by the Registry, redeemable for licensed Compiles and hired castings. Gold near the core; waste paper past the Marches — its worth reaches exactly as far as the Registry's arm."),
            (en: "Source-Trade", cn: "鬻源",
             zh: "思維不可授，源碼可鬻（卷二）。譜系近原典者昂，分支屢歧者賤。有照者出行會領，無照者流分支底層——同源二市，其價十倍之差。",
             tr: "A Programme cannot be handed over; source can be sold (Vol. II). Lineage near the original commands a price; a much-Forked line goes cheap. The licensed flows from the Guildreach, the unlicensed through the Underfork — one source, two markets, tenfold apart in price."),
            (en: "Cast-for-Hire", cn: "代發",
             zh: "覺醒者受值而發思維——療疾、築城、護商、征戰。其價隨域載與天氣而動（卷十二）：潮壅之日，一發千金。",
             tr: "A Booted casts for pay — healing, raising walls, warding caravans, making war. The price moves with field density and the weather (Vol. XII): on a day of congested tide, one casting is worth a thousand in gold."),
            (en: "Bounty", cn: "賞格",
             zh: "註冊局懸格緝病毒、盜版與行注入者。抗體之糧餉，盡出於此——故抗體所巡，恆在賞格所厚之地。",
             tr: "The Registry sets prices on Viruses, pirates, and wielders of Injection. The Antibody's bread comes wholly from this — which is why their patrols run thickest where the bounties run richest."),
            (en: "Traceless Labor", cn: "無痕之役",
             zh: "凡握手必入察錄（卷十五）——唯已卸載者行而無痕。或問：何不僱凡民？曰：凡民有名可審、有沉睡之記憶體可植、有一朝啟動而盡譯所聞之危；幽存無憶可讀、無名可錄。凡民賤，幽存不可讀——所鬻者非工，乃不可讀也。凡不欲書於錄者之事，皆其業也。此幽存獨佔之市，諸派陰用而陽不認。",
             tr: "Every Handshake enters the Log (Vol. XV) — only the Uninstalled act and leave no trace. Why not simply hire the common? Because a commoner has a name that can be interrogated, a sleeping Memory that can be planted, and the standing peril of one day Booting — whereupon all they once perceived compiles. A Ghost has no Memory to read and no name in any roll. The common are cheap; the Ghosts are unreadable — and what they sell is not labor, but unreadability. Whatever must not be written in the record is their trade: the Ghosts' one monopoly, used by every faction in the dark, acknowledged by none in the light."),
        ]),
    ],
)
